From: Runeon Contributors <dev@runeon.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Do not unwind past StackBase after a collided unwind.

The x64 handler search checks the return address slot at Rsp against
StackBase before each unwind, so a misread frame near the top of the
stack ends the search with EXCEPTION_STACK_INVALID instead of faulting
in RtlVirtualUnwind2(). A handler that returns ExceptionCollidedUnwind
skips that check: unwind_exception_handler() has replaced the context
with the one of the unwind it collided with, and call_seh_handlers()
unwinds it directly and jumps past the check. When that context leaves
Rsp less than one slot below StackBase or above it, the leaf unwind
reads past the thread stack, and the resulting access violation fails
the same way until the process dies in RtlVirtualUnwind2().

Apply the same check in both collided-unwind branches, for language
handlers and for TEB frame handlers, and end the search the way the
loop does when the check fails: mark the exception
EXCEPTION_STACK_INVALID and return STATUS_UNHANDLED_EXCEPTION, which
leaves the existing unhandled exception path to the caller.

This only stops these two entries from unwinding once the return
address slot is past StackBase. It does not check the lower stack
limit, page accessibility or other reads during the unwind, and the
collided-unwind branches of RtlUnwindEx() are unchanged.

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/signal_x86_64.c b/dlls/ntdll/signal_x86_64.c
index ce263e3..f8364a2 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/signal_x86_64.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/signal_x86_64.c
@@ -309,6 +309,15 @@ NTSTATUS call_seh_handlers( EXCEPTION_RECORD *rec, CONTEXT *orig_context )
                 TRACE( "nested exception\n" );
                 break;
             case ExceptionCollidedUnwind:
+                /* the handler restored the collided unwind's context, which
+                 * the check at the top of the loop has not seen */
+                if (!is_valid_unwind_rsp( context.Rsp ))
+                {
+                    ERR( "invalid stack pointer %p after collided unwind (%p-%p)\n", (void *)context.Rsp,
+                         NtCurrentTeb()->Tib.StackLimit, NtCurrentTeb()->Tib.StackBase );
+                    rec->ExceptionFlags |= EXCEPTION_STACK_INVALID;
+                    return STATUS_UNHANDLED_EXCEPTION;
+                }
                 RtlVirtualUnwind( UNW_FLAG_NHANDLER, dispatch.ImageBase, dispatch.ControlPc,
                                   dispatch.FunctionEntry, &context, NULL, &frame, NULL );
                 goto unwind_done;
@@ -340,6 +349,13 @@ NTSTATUS call_seh_handlers( EXCEPTION_RECORD *rec, CONTEXT *orig_context )
                 TRACE( "nested exception\n" );
                 break;
             case ExceptionCollidedUnwind:
+                if (!is_valid_unwind_rsp( context.Rsp ))
+                {
+                    ERR( "invalid stack pointer %p after collided TEB unwind (%p-%p)\n", (void *)context.Rsp,
+                         NtCurrentTeb()->Tib.StackLimit, NtCurrentTeb()->Tib.StackBase );
+                    rec->ExceptionFlags |= EXCEPTION_STACK_INVALID;
+                    return STATUS_UNHANDLED_EXCEPTION;
+                }
                 RtlVirtualUnwind( UNW_FLAG_NHANDLER, dispatch.ImageBase, dispatch.ControlPc,
                                   dispatch.FunctionEntry, &context, NULL, &frame, NULL );
                 teb_frame = teb_frame->Prev;
